<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="097" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>SECURITY: /api/communications/send attaches any document and links any record without checking the caller — authorize both per item, and fix the outbound archive writing a document id into sprk_graphitemid</title>
    <phase>6 UAT round 3-4 (2026-10-03/04)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization change on a live BFF route (`.cs`), plus a data-correctness fix and tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security: a per-item authorization gap reachable by every signed-in user; must reuse the existing evaluators exactly and fail closed.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the shared Communication module (`Services/Communication/**`, `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs`, `Api/Filters/CommunicationAuthorizationFilter.cs`) — run `/conflict-check` first; other projects (email-communication-intelligence-r2) own this surface.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>096</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, authorization, communication, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Found by task 096's code review (2026-10-04, `notes/096-email-tab.md`); owner decision the same day: *"Fix it here before shipping"* and fix the archive bug in the same task. The Word Email tab (096) ships in the same deploy as this fix.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE BFF security engineer: endpoint-filter authorization (ADR-008), OBO vs app-only access (ADR-028), SPE file access (ADR-007).</role>

  <goal>RE-SCOPED 2026-10-06 (owner decision option 1, notes/097 §6; owner go 2026-10-06: "uac-r2 task 161 is working so you can proceed with completing the dependent work"). The send authorization is unified-access-control-r2 task 161's (`Api/Filters/CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter.cs`, on master via #1312, d254d7166) and is NOT rebuilt here. This task: (1) fixes the outbound archive (it wrote the `sprk_document` id and the archive container into the pointer fields, so the archived row named no file) — REVISED by owner OPTION A, 2026-10-06 (notes §9): each attachment is saved to SPE as its OWN NEW file in the communication's container and the archived `sprk_document` points at that file, as inbound archiving does (never the source document's file, which would make two rows share one), keeping UAC-r2 task 146's owner behaviour; (2) switches the Word Email tab on in the deploy workflow (`ADDIN_EMAIL_TAB_ENABLED: "true"`; the code default stays off); (3) records, by reading 161's filter, that the Word Email tab's request passes it; (4) leaves the live checks open for the main session.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **The gap (096 review)**: `CommunicationAuthorizationFilter` (`Api/Filters/CommunicationAuthorizationFilter.cs`) only
        requires an authenticated caller with an `oid`. `CommunicationService` downloads each `AttachmentDocumentIds` entry
        with the **app's** identity (`CommunicationService.cs` ~`:1074`/`:1427` → the attachment fetch) and never checks
        that the caller can read the `sprk_document`. `Associations` are written to the `sprk_communication` row
        (`MapAssociationFieldsAsync`, ~`:874`) without checking the caller's access to those records. So any signed-in user
        can email any document by id and file an email against any record — an IDOR, on both the `User` and `SharedMailbox`
        send modes.
      - **Reuse the existing evaluators — do not invent new ones**: per-document Read — the repo's document access check
        (`DocumentAuthorizationFilter` / `IAiAuthorizationService` per-document, or `CallerRecordAccessProbe` +
        `OperationAccessPolicy` as tasks 064/084 used; `SpeFileStore.DownloadFileAsUserAsync` is the reviewer's suggestion
        for reading the file AS the user). Per-record link — the same probe/policy the Office paths use for filing
        (`entity.associate_document`-style AppendTo, task 084's `EvaluateFilingAccessAsync` shape, or the read gate task 064
        used for To Do sources — choose and justify). Denied and not-found must be indistinguishable (task 064's rule).
      - **The archive bug**: with `ArchiveToSpe` on, the outbound archive writes a `sprk_document` id into
        `sprk_graphitemid` (096 note). Find the write (around `:446-480` and `ArchiveToSpeAsync`), fix it to store the Graph
        item id, regression-test it.
      - **Callers to keep working**: the Spaarke email page (`SendEmailPage` / `EmailComposer`), the Word Email tab (096,
        `SendMode.User`, one attachment = the user's own saved document, one association = its record), any server/AI caller
        of `CommunicationService` (find them — an app-only internal caller must not start failing; decide per caller and state
        it).
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Authorization happens before any mail is sent: refuse the whole request (403, a stable error code, the offending item NOT named when that would confirm existence) if any attachment or association is not permitted. Fail closed when the check itself fails (503/500 — never send).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">User-initiated sends are authorized as the caller (OBO identity / caller probe). Do not widen any role; do not add app-only reads to make a check pass.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">Reuse the existing access evaluators named in the background; no new authorization service. If none fits, ESCALATE (trigger 1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">`/send-bulk` gets the same checks (shared code path) — verify, do not assume.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF obligations: placement stated; publish size owed to the main session (this worktree is not comparable); CVE check; `/conflict-check` before editing the Communication module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests in KEEP paths: contract tests for the route (caller CAN read → 200; CANNOT read one attachment → 403 and no send; association not permitted → 403 and no send; probe failure → fail closed), a seeded negative control (remove the check → the 403 tests fail), and a regression test for the archive field. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <!-- RE-SCOPED 2026-10-06. The original ten criteria are kept verbatim in <notes> as history. -->
    <!-- ARCHIVE criteria REVISED 2026-10-06 for owner OPTION A (notes/097 §9). The earlier criterion "the archived row stores the SOURCE document's drive/item ids" is SUPERSEDED: it made two rows share one SPE file (notes §7.1). -->
    <criterion testable="true">Archive (option A): with ArchiveToSpe on, each outbound attachment is saved to SharePoint Embedded as its OWN NEW file — the bytes the send already read, one upload per attachment, through `SpeFileStore` — in the communication's container (the same `CommunicationContainerResolver` decision as the `.eml` and the inbound archive), named `{communicationId:N}_{sanitized name}`; the archived `sprk_document` stores THAT upload's item id and container (never the source document's item, never a `sprk_document` id), is linked by `sprk_relatedcommunication`, and gets the Document Profile job. Both send modes (SharedMailbox and User).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Never two rows on one file: a name repeated within one send gets its own path, and an archive upload never replaces an existing file (`ConflictBehavior.Fail`). The source document's file is never written, moved or deleted. An upload that returns no item creates no row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invariants kept: task 146's owner (`ResolveContentOwnerAsync` / `ApplyContentOwner`, refusal → nothing uploaded or created); best-effort semantics (the email is already sent; any archive failure is logged and never fails the send).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Regression tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`): red on the old code and on the superseded shared-pointer draft, green on the fix, seeded removals bite (outputs recorded in notes §10.3); a &gt;4 MB attachment goes through the same upload inbound uses (inbound has no upload-session path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`.github/workflows/deploy-office-addins.yml` sets `ADDIN_EMAIL_TAB_ENABLED: "true"` with a comment citing 161 on master (#1312) and the owner go of 2026-10-06; `webpack.config.js` keeps the default OFF and its comment says the workflow turns it on; `.env.example` no longer says "held off".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/097 §7 records, from reading 161's filter, which checks run for the Word Email tab's request (sendMode User, the user's own document as the attachment, the document's record as the association) and why they pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: `/conflict-check`; build 0/0; Communication + Office test scopes and ArchTests green; no new HIGH CVE; publish size master vs branch from fresh short-path worktrees (equal file counts); inline code-review + adr-check.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">Live (main session, after deploy): the Word Email tab sends the user's own document; a foreign document id is refused with `sdap.access.deny.communication.send`. Left OPEN by this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>No existing evaluator can answer "may this caller read document X / link record Y" for these entity types — STOP and report; a new authorization service is a design decision for the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>An existing internal (server/AI) caller of `CommunicationService` legitimately sends documents the initiating user cannot read — STOP and report it before changing its behaviour.</trigger>
    <trigger>`/conflict-check` shows another active project editing these Communication files — coordinate before editing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>`/conflict-check`; read the filter, the service's attachment/association/archive paths, and every caller.</step>
    <step>Reproduce the gap in a contract test first (it must pass a send it should refuse).</step>
    <step>Add the per-attachment Read and per-association link checks using existing evaluators; fail closed; tests; seeded control.</step>
    <step>Fix the archive field; regression test.</step>
    <step>Gates; `notes/097-communications-send-authorization.md`; POML status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The send route, the per-document and per-record access evaluators (tasks 032/064/084) and the user-context file read (`SpeFileStore.DownloadFileAsUserAsync`) exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — adds checks to the existing route using existing evaluators, and corrects one field write. No new route or service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any signed-in user can email any Spaarke document by id and file mail against any record; the Word Email tab would ship as a new caller of that hole.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

